    "text": "\n\nA public system, often referred to as a public service, is a government-operated organization designed to provide essential goods, services, or facilities to the general public. These systems are funded by taxes, which are collected from citizens and businesses.\n\nLet's take the example of a public library. A public library system is a network of libraries funded by the government, usually at the city, county, or state level. Citizens can visit these libraries to borrow books, DVDs, and other media, use computers and Wi-Fi, attend educational programs, and access various resources.\n\nThe library system has a staff responsible for managing the collection, checking out materials, maintaining the building, and providing customer service. The staff also coordinates with other libraries in the system to ensure resources are shared effectively and efficiently",
